# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide demonstrates a minimal working example of the `qiskit-paulice` package. We use [spacetime Pauli checks](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725) to detect errors during execution of a Clifford circuit, then postselect only samples for which no error was detected. For a more explanatory end-to-end workflow that quantifies the fidelity improvement, see the [in-depth tutorial](/tutorials/spacetime-codes).\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini menunjukkan contoh kerja minimum bagi pakej `qiskit-paulice`. Kami menggunakan [semakan Pauli ruang-masa](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725) untuk mengesan ralat semasa pelaksanaan litar Clifford, kemudian memilih lepas (postselect) hanya sampel yang tiada ralat dikesan. Untuk aliran kerja hujung-ke-hujung yang lebih terperinci yang mengukur peningkatan fidelity, lihat [tutorial mendalam](/tutorials/spacetime-codes).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Workflow steps**\n"
"1. Prepare the inputs: a Clifford payload circuit, the target/ancilla qubits to host checks, and a noise model.\n"
"2. Find good spacetime Pauli checks and add them to the circuit.\n"
"3. Sample the checked circuit.\n"
"4. Postselect only the samples for which no error was detected.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah aliran kerja**\n"
"1. Sediakan input: litar muatan Clifford, qubit sasaran/ancilla untuk menempatkan semakan, dan model hingar.\n"
"2. Cari semakan Pauli ruang-masa yang baik dan tambahkannya ke litar.\n"
"3. Sampel litar yang telah disemak.\n"
"4. Pilih lepas hanya sampel yang tiada ralat dikesan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Prepare the inputs {#1-prepare-the-inputs}"
msgstr "1. Sediakan input {#1-prepare-the-inputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`add_pauli_checks` takes a Clifford **circuit** ending in measurements (or, with the `stabilizers` kwarg, one with no measurements, as in the [spacetime codes guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice/guides/low-overhead-error-detection-using-spacetime-codes)), the **target qubits** that will be used to implement checks, and a **noise model** used to score candidate checks. Here we build a shallow random Clifford circuit, lay it out on a 1D chain of physical qubits on `ibm_boston`, pair each payload qubit with a neighboring ancilla (so a check needs no SWAP gates), and infer a rough depolarizing noise model from backend benchmark data.\n"
msgstr "`add_pauli_checks` menerima **litar** Clifford yang berakhir dengan pengukuran (atau, dengan kwarg `stabilizers`, litar tanpa pengukuran, seperti dalam [panduan kod ruang-masa](/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice/guides/low-overhead-error-detection-using-spacetime-codes)), **qubit sasaran** yang akan digunakan untuk melaksanakan semakan, dan **model hingar** yang digunakan untuk menilai calon semakan. Di sini kami membina litar Clifford rawak yang cetek, menempatkannya pada rantaian 1D qubit fizikal pada `ibm_boston`, memasangkan setiap qubit muatan dengan ancilla jiran (supaya semakan tidak memerlukan gate SWAP), dan menyimpulkan model hingar depolarizing kasar daripada data penanda aras backend.\n"

